cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use TikiTorch, cite the software release and the focused paper that
  owns the research result you rely on.
title: "TikiTorch: PyTorch-shaped infrastructure for tropical deep learning"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "TikiTorch Authors"
version: 0.2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/nyuolab/tikitorch"
url: "https://github.com/nyuolab/tikitorch"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
abstract: >-
  TikiTorch is a PyTorch-shaped research library for max-plus, min-plus,
  morphological, dyadic, and hard-routed deep learning. It includes operators,
  modules, model families, optimizers, recipe-scoped closure audits, exact
  selected-VJP replay for supported route traces, and FPGA research artifacts.
keywords:
  - tropical deep learning
  - max-plus algebra
  - min-plus algebra
  - morphological neural networks
  - hard routing
  - FPGA learning
